Hi,
I haven written regarding this issues before. So maybe it sounds familiar=20
:-)

I'm unable to produce a booting image when combining a machine from the=20
meta-intel layer with "DISTRO ?=3D "poky-ivi-systemd" from the meta-ivi=20
layer.
You will find a photograph of my screen attached, but I will describe the=20
error anyway.


Which error do I get?

When I'm booting my image the machine fails to boot. The relevant=20
information (IMHO) are the lines:
        /init: line 98: mount: not found
        /init: line 98: mount: not found
        /init: line 98: mount: not found
and
        cat: can't open '/proc/cmdline': No such file or directory
        Waiting for removable media...


When does the error occur?

Every image built with the local.conf options
MACHINE ?=3D "crownbay"   OR      MACHINE ?=3D "chiefriver"
AND
DISTRO ?=3D "poky-ivi-systemd"

failed to boot.

I have tried builds with meta-ivi excalibur (not 100% sure) and foton=20
releases and the master branch aswell
Similar applies to poky and meta-intel. I tried the danny and dylan=20
releases and the master branch.

The boot happens from an USB stick on which I dd'ed=20
"foton-image-$MACHINE-$BUILDDATE.hddimg"

All other builds are booting fine.

Addind "EXTRA=5FIMAGE=5FFEATURE =3D "udev-extraconf" did not change this=20
behauviour.

Building only with meta-intel OR meta-ivi results in a booting image.

So, any ideas?

regards,

